      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "I'm not a medical professional, but I can try to help. If you suspect you have low blood sugar, it's generally recommended to wait until you can take a glucose meal or snack, such as a small serving of glucose tablets, hard candies, or a single-serve pack of juice, to help stabilize your blood sugar levels. Taking insulin without being instructed to do so can be confusing and potentially hazardous. If you're unsure, consider contacting a registered dietitian, certified diabetes educator, or a healthcare provider who can provide personalized guidance. They can help you manage your symptoms safely and efficiently.",
